{"term":"limp-dick","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"phallic_inadequacy","concept":"phallic_inadequacy_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":8,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A contemptible, cowardly, or ineffectual person; evokes erectile dysfunction as a metaphor for weakness, failure, or lack of resolve.","english_term":"limp-dick","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"More sexually explicit than 'dickless' because it references erectile dysfunction specifically rather than absence; functions as both noun ('he's a limp-dick') and adjective ('a limp-dick policy')."}
{"term":"small-dick energy","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"phallic_inadequacy","concept":"small_dick_energy","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":60,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":2019,"regional":null,"definition":"An internet-era phrase describing insecure, overcompensating, or bullying behavior metaphorically attributed to anxiety about having a small penis.","english_term":"small-dick energy","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Emerged as the inversion of 'big dick energy' (BDE), which itself was popularized in 2018; used across genders to describe behavioral patterns rather than literal anatomy; notably more acceptable in mainstream media than most phallic insults."}
{"term":"dick-rider","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"sycophancy","concept":"dick_rider_sycophant","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":75,"peak_year":null,"regional":"US","definition":"A sycophant or uncritical fanboy who idolizes someone; also deployed as a homophobic slur implying the target performs oral or anal sex on the person they admire.","english_term":"dick-rider","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Dual register: in hip-hop slang it primarily means sycophant (circa 1990s onward); in homophobic contexts it literalizes the sexual imagery; recognition concentrated in younger urban US demographics."}
{"term":"cuck","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"cuckoldry","concept":"cuck","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":68,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":87,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":2016,"regional":null,"definition":"Shortened form of 'cuckold'; an internet and far-right slur for a man perceived as weak, emasculated, or politically submissive, especially one who tolerates humiliation from women or political opponents.","english_term":"cuckold","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Derived from cuckold fetish communities (where men eroticize their partner having sex with others) and weaponized as a political insult c. 2015–2016; peak use in alt-right rhetoric around the 2016 US election; now general internet shorthand for any perceived submissive male."}
{"term":"simp","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"male_deference","concept":"simp","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":28,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":96,"peak_year":2020,"regional":null,"definition":"A man who is excessively attentive, deferential, or servile toward a woman in the hope of gaining sexual access or romantic approval.","english_term":"simp","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Originally 1990s hip-hop slang ('sucker idolizing mediocre pussy'); revived by incel and manosphere communities c. 2018 and exploded mainstream via TikTok in 2019–2020; now broadly recognized across age groups."}
{"term":"incel","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"involuntary_celibacy","concept":"incel","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":22,"technical":18,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":2018,"regional":null,"definition":"'Involuntary celibate'; a man who attributes his inability to have sex to women's choices and society's structural unfairness rather than his own behavior, typically with expressed resentment or misogyny.","english_term":"incel","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Coined 1997 by a Canadian woman as a neutral self-description; hijacked by misogynistic online forums c. 2014; entered mainstream after violence attributed to incel ideology (2018 Toronto van attack); now functions simultaneously as self-identification, community label, and slur."}
{"term":"virgin (as insult)","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"sexual_inexperience","concept":"virgin_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":18,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":2018,"regional":null,"definition":"'Virgin' repurposed as a pejorative implying the target is naive, socially incompetent, or pitiful, with their sexual inexperience standing as evidence of broader social failure.","english_term":"virgin","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The literal word predates internet culture by centuries; its use as a pure social insult (divorced from literal sexual status) peaked in meme culture c. 2016–2018, especially the 'Virgin vs. Chad' meme format; the insult relies on treating virginity as shameful rather than virtuous."}
{"term":"beta","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"manosphere_hierarchy","concept":"manosphere_male_hierarchy","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":20,"technical":12,"recognition_pct_current":83,"recognition_pct_peak":87,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"In manosphere discourse, a man who is submissive, non-dominant, or romantically unattractive; the opposite of 'alpha'; used as an insult for perceived weakness, social passivity, or failure to attract women.","english_term":"beta male","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Borrowed from debunked wolf-pack dominance research; foundational to incel, red-pill, and pick-up artist ideology; widely used mockingly by mainstream culture to satirize that same ideology."}
{"term":"alpha","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"manosphere_hierarchy","concept":"manosphere_male_hierarchy","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":12,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":91,"recognition_pct_peak":91,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"In manosphere discourse, a sexually dominant, confident, high-status man who attracts women without visible effort; valorized within the subculture but widely mocked outside it as a self-flattering fantasy.","english_term":"alpha male","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Used sincerely in pick-up artist and red-pill communities; used ironically by mainstream and feminist commentary; the term's double life (sincere/ironic) makes crude/register scores context-dependent; no single peak year because it remains actively in use."}
{"term":"omega","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"manosphere_hierarchy","concept":"manosphere_male_hierarchy","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":22,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":60,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"In manosphere discourse, the lowest-status male, below even the 'beta'; considered sexually invisible, socially irrelevant, and without realistic hope of female attention.","english_term":"omega male","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Less widely recognized than 'alpha' or 'beta'; primarily circulates within incel and red-pill communities; the Greek-letter hierarchy (alpha > beta > delta > gamma > omega) has multiple variants across different manosphere factions."}
{"term":"whipped","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"partner_dominance","concept":"partner_controlled_male","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":22,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":94,"recognition_pct_peak":94,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A man so controlled or dominated by his romantic or sexual partner that he abandons his own preferences, friendships, or dignity to please her.","english_term":"whipped","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Shortening of 'pussy-whipped'; the crude origin is largely forgotten in everyday use; mild enough to appear in mainstream TV and film; widely understood across age groups and genders."}
{"term":"henpecked","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"partner_dominance","concept":"partner_controlled_male","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":14,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A man nagged, dominated, and controlled by his wife; a mid-20th-century domestic term evoking a hen (female chicken) pecking a subordinate rooster.","english_term":"henpecked","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Largely displaced by 'whipped' in contemporary usage; survives in passive recognition and period fiction; the agricultural metaphor dates to at least the 17th century; peak recognition predates living memory so peak_year is set null."}
{"term":"pussy-whipped","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"partner_dominance","concept":"partner_controlled_male","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":82,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":87,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A man so driven by desire for his partner's sexual approval that he submits entirely to her will; the vulgar root form of 'whipped,' making the genital reference explicit.","english_term":"whipped","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Pussy' refers to female genitalia; the metaphor implies sexual desire as a leash; considered significantly cruder than plain 'whipped' due to the explicit anatomical reference; still in active use despite the softer 'whipped' being more socially acceptable."}
{"term":"emasculated","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"emasculation","concept":"emasculation","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"literary","crude":22,"technical":42,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Having been stripped of male power, authority, or sexuality; rendered weak, ineffectual, or feminized, either literally (castration) or—far more commonly—figuratively.","english_term":"emasculated","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Distinctly more formal/literary than other terms in this section; common in political commentary, psychology, and sociology; the literal meaning (surgical castration) is almost never invoked; the figurative use dominates entirely in modern English."}
{"term":"himbo","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"attractiveness_intellect","concept":"himbo","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":18,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":2020,"regional":null,"definition":"An attractive but unintelligent man; the male counterpart to 'bimbo,' often used affectionately for a good-natured, sexually appealing man without intellectual depth.","english_term":"himbo","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Blend of 'him' + 'bimbo'; unlike 'bimbo,' which is frequently cruel and derogatory, 'himbo' is often celebratory or affectionate, especially in queer and feminist online spaces; peaked in mainstream visibility c. 2019–2021 as a cultural archetype."}
{"term":"dumb slut","lang":"en","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":90,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A compound insult attacking a woman's intelligence and sexual morality simultaneously; 'dumb' functions as an amplifier for 'slut,' framing the target as both promiscuous and too stupid to recognize her own degradation.","english_term":"dumb slut","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Slut' carries most of the semantic weight; 'dumb' intensifies by adding contempt for the target's cognition; the pairing is common enough to function as a stock phrase rather than a novel coinage; directed almost exclusively at women."}
